==English==
{{rfquote|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|contravenir|lang=frm}} (French {{term|contrevenir|lang=fr}}), from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|contraveniō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌkɒn.tɹəˈviːn/|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|contraven}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[act]] [[contrary]] to an [[order]], or [[fail]] to [[conform]] to a [[regulation]].
#*{{quote-news
|year=2012
|date=May 24
|author=Adam Gabbatt
|title=Canada student protests erupt into political crisis with mass arrests
|work=the Guardian
|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/world/2012/may/24/canada-student-fee-protest-arrests?INTCMP=SRCH
|page=
|passage=Some legal experts argue that the bill '''contravenes''' Canada's charter of rights and freedoms. Montreal constitutional lawyer Julius Grey told the Vancouver Sun that Bill 78 was "flagrantly unconstitutional".}}
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[deny]] the [[truth]] of something.

